# Generated React naming

When creating or editing generated GrapeJS projects (`generator/`, `projects/`):

## Rules

| What | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Route key in `site.json` | `kebab-case` | `hello-world` |
| React component | `PascalCase`, prefix `Page` | `PageHelloWorld` |
| Page file | `PascalCase.tsx` (matches component) | `PageHelloWorld.tsx` |
| Layout components | `PascalCase` | `SiteLayout`, `SiteHeader` |
| Folders | `kebab-case` or lowercase | `components/layout`, `grape` |

## Never

- Hyphens in component or file names (`PageHello-world` ❌)
- camelCase for React components (`pageHelloWorld` ❌)
- Mismatch between import path and file name

## Generator

Use `generator/lib/names.ts`:

- `pageKeyToComponent(key)` → `PageHelloWorld`
- `pageKeyToFileName(key)` → `PageHelloWorld.tsx`
- `toPascalCase(segment)` for each `-` / `_` separated part

Nested routes use `__` in keys (`about/team` → `about__team` → `PageAboutTeam`).
